  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-review-threads",
      "text": "[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-review-threads)\n[](https://www.npmjs.com/package/dsh-review-threads)\n[](https://github.com/huandu/dsh-review-threads/actions/workflows/verify.yml)\n[](https://github.com/topics/dsh-plugin)\n[](LICENSE)\n\nPersistent, GitHub-style review threads for DeepSeek Harness diffs."
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-review-threads",
      "text": "`dsh-review-threads` takes over the official `changes-review` tab and keeps the\nofficial turn diff data source. A Review is bound to a diff and owns many\nline-level Threads. User draft changes become visible to AI only when the user\nsubmits a Review. AI can add comments immediately, but cannot delete or resolve\nthreads."
    },
    {
      "section": "Status",
      "text": "Version `0.1.1` is the current release. DeepSeek Harness itself remains in preview,\nso review the compatibility range before installing."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- DeepSeek Harness `0.2.1-rc.1` through `0.2.1`\n- Node.js 22.18 or newer\n- Git for committed revision reviews"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile web add dsh-review-threads\n```\n\nRestart the profile after installation. Removing the plugin restores the\nofficial Review tab; review data stays under the profile's DSH storage."
    },
    {
      "section": "Review commands",
      "text": "- `/review` opens the current working-tree changes, including untracked files.\n- `/review <base>..<head>` opens a committed revision range. Use\n  `/review <base>...<head>` for merge-base comparison.\n- Append `-- <paths...>` to limit either comparison to repository paths.\n- Use `/review bind <base>..<head>` to open a range whose patch matches the\n  current session's working Review; confirm the bind in the panel.\n- `/review-diagnostics` reports storage counts without comment bodies.\n- `/review-clear-drafts` discards unsubmitted drafts in the current session."
    },
    {
      "section": "Review commands",
      "text": "The command only opens the Review panel. It does not send a conversation\nmessage or start an AI turn."
    },
    {
      "section": "Releases",
      "text": "Creating a non-prerelease GitHub Release for a tag matching the package version\nruns `.github/workflows/publish.yml`. The workflow verifies the repository,\nbuilds the package, and publishes through the npm Trusted Publisher connection;\nno npm token is stored in GitHub."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install\npnpm verify\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "- [Requirements](docs/requirements/requirements.md)\n- [Design](docs/design.md)\n- [Development plan](docs/development-plan.md)\n- [Compatibility](docs/compatibility.md)\n- [Decisions](docs/decisions/)"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
